            <ArticleTitle>Cancer Death Rate Down 25% Since 1991.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>OF2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1158/2159-8290.CD-NB2017-010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Death rates from cancer dropped by 25% from 1991 to 2014, driven by declines in smoking and improvements in detection and treatment methods, according to a new report from the American Cancer Society. However, significant gender and racial disparities remain for incidence and death rates for many cancers.</AbstractText>
